<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35473" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">persĕcūtor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A pursuer</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flagitiorum turpium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Capitol. Alb. 11, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A persecutor</i> of Christians, Mort. Persec. 1;
					<i><span class="en">id. Inst. 5, 23, 1</span></i>: Ecclesiae,
			Hieron. Ep. ad Helv. 3: sub ense persecutoris pati, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 1, 28; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Tim.
				1, 13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>A prosecutor</i>, <i>plaintiff</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Dig.
				48, 3, 7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
